# Table Selection Action Parity

In sidebar directory/list workspaces, every record action exposed on a **table
row** (desktop row buttons, mobile row actions, or row overflow menu) must also
be available on the **selection header** (`TableSelectionToolbar` /
`TableSelectionBar`) when rows are selected — **except View**.

**View is via row click/tap**, not the selection header. Do not pass `onView` to
`TableSelectionToolbar` / `TableSelectionBar` (those props were removed).

Do not leave other actions only on the row. Selection is a first-class way to
act on records; the header must offer the same non-view set.

## Rules

1. **Parity** — If a user can Edit / Delete / Print / Map / Sync / etc. from a
   row, wire the same capability into `TableSelectionToolbar` (`onEdit`,
   `onDelete`, and/or `actions`). Do **not** add a selection-header View button.
2. **Selection validity** — Show only actions that make sense for the current
   selection:
   - **Single-select only** (Edit, “create from this record”, …): render when
     `selectedCount === 1`; **hide** when multi-select (do not leave a
     permanently disabled control cluttering the bar).
   - **Multi-select capable** (Delete, Print, bulk status, …): show for
     `selectedCount >= 1`.
   - Shared standard Edit already disables when `selectedCount !== 1` inside
     `TableSelectionBar`; feature `actions` should **hide** single-only buttons
     instead of always rendering them disabled.
3. **Permissions / feature gates** — Still honor `canEdit` / `canDelete` and
   feature flags. Hide actions the user cannot use, same as the row.
4. **Same handler semantics** — Selection actions should call the same open /
   mutate helpers as the row (e.g. `openEditX(selected[0])`, bulk delete with
   all selected ids). Do not invent a second code path with different behavior.
5. **Mobile + desktop** — If the workspace has both a desktop table and a mobile
   list, keep row actions and both selection toolbars in sync (still excluding
   View from the selection header).

```tsx
// ✅ GOOD — row action also on selection header; View omitted (row click opens view)
<TableSelectionToolbar
  selectedIds={selectedIds}
  pageRowIds={pageIds}
  onSelectedIdsChange={setSelectedIds}
  onEdit={() => selected[0] && openEdit(selected[0])}
  onDelete={() => requestDelete(selected)}
  canEdit={canUpdate}
  canDelete={canDelete}
  actions={
    <>
      {selectedIds.length === 1 && canCreateInvoice ? (
        <Button /* create invoice from selected[0] */ />
      ) : null}
      <Button /* print — valid for single and multi */ />
    </>
  }
/>
```

```tsx
// ❌ BAD — print/sync only on the row; selection header has Edit/Delete only
<TableSelectionToolbar onEdit={…} onDelete={…} />
// row still has Print / Retry sync / Map with no selection equivalents
```

## Checklist

- [ ] Every non-view row action has a selection-header counterpart
- [ ] Selection header has no View button (row click/tap opens view)
- [ ] Single-only actions hidden when `selectedCount !== 1`
- [ ] Multi actions work on the full selection
- [ ] Permission gates match the row
- [ ] Desktop and mobile selection bars stay aligned
